      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Toronto's season is a jagged tale of brilliance and collapse, and the latest chapter left fans reeling. <strong>The Blue Jays suffered an 11-0 demolition by the Mariners on July 4, a game where Shane Bieber crumbled with seven runs in four innings and the team recorded just one hit</strong>. Yet, just hours earlier, they blanked the same Mariners 2-0 behind Dylan Cease's seven shutout innings, proving the team's swing-to-swing volatility. At 42-47 and 11.5 games behind in the AL East, the Jays are stuck in third, their one-game win streak now overshadowed by that nine-run implosion. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. remains the story, even as he declined an All-Star invite - a quiet rebuke of the spotlight while Cease and Varland head to Seattle. <strong>Now, the finale looms tonight at 5:00 PM ET against the Mariners, where Trey Yesavage must stabilize a series that's already slipped away</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
